<h1>Charles Schwab Assessment Prototype</h1>

<p>
    This submission is a <strong>Blazor-hosted, API-first prototype</strong> that combines a URL shortener
    with an agentic workflow orchestration engine.
</p>

<p>
    The current UI is intentionally lightweight. The primary reviewer surface is the minimal API layer,
    which exposes URL management, analytics, workflow execution, approvals, and replanning behavior.
</p>

<h2>Key capabilities</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Shorten URLs with optional aliases and expiration</li>
    <li>Inspect redirect analytics</li>
    <li>Start, resume, safe-stop, and replan workflow runs</li>
    <li>Enforce approval gates and policy guardrails</li>
    <li>Track audit trail and reliability-oriented workflow metrics</li>
</ul>

<h2>Reviewer guidance</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Read <code>README.md</code> for setup and endpoint details</li>
    <li>Read <code>ARCHITECTURE.md</code> for system and orchestration design</li>
    <li>Read <code>SCENARIOS.md</code> for greenfield, brownfield, and ambiguous flows</li>
    <li>Read <code>TESTING.md</code> and <code>ENGINEERING_SUMMARY.md</code> for validation and final rationale</li>
</ul>
